{
  "metadata": {
    "description": "ChampSim configuration approximating one socket of this server: Intel Xeon Gold 6548Y+ with 32 physical cores, SMT disabled, and one socket-local LLC domain.",
    "created_for": "cache-to-scratchpad switching latency evaluation",
    "observed_on": "2026-04-17",
    "modeling_notes": [
      "This file models one socket only: 32 online physical cores sharing one 60 MiB LLC.",
      "ChampSim does not model hardware coherence, so this is intended for cache/scratchpad switching-cost approximation rather than a coherence-complete model.",
      "The host exposes two populated DDR5 DIMMs on socket 0 via EDAC, so physical_memory.channels is set to 2.",
      "DDR5 data rate is set to the processor-supported 5200 MT/s because SPD timing data was not readable from this user account.",
      "LLC bandwidth parameters are aggregate approximations for a 32-slice socket LLC rather than a literal single-bank cache."
    ]
  },

